			<div class="content" id="post-content-4818621">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Special Containment Procedures, Description, Discovery Notes, Journal Entries, Test Notes, Incident Report</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A dark take on getting a bad back from an old mattress. After a grisly murder where a child's spine was torn out of her body (and is missing), crime scene investigators noted the lack of blood on her twin size mattress, although the sheets were saturated. The SCP Foundation secures the mattress as SCP-XXXX. But what if the mattress itself isn't the problem?</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Journal entries describe the following story: a mom gets a mattress from a freecycling site when her older daughter is ready for a &quot;big girl bed.&quot; The child first complains that her mattress is bumpy, then that it moves at night, and finally runs into her room after dreaming about a skeletal creature in her mattress that &quot;wants my back, because its back hurts.&quot; The mom lets the girl sleep with her that night, but insists that the little girl sleeps in her own bed the following night. The next night the child is killed and the journal is confiscated along with the mattress. Research reveals nothing unusual in mattress's history, and no clear explanation for how it became anomalous.</p>
<p>After recovery of SCP-XXXX, months of tests show that any vertebrate (living or dead, human or non-human) suffers the same fate. There are 26 distinct lumps in the mattress, (the same as the number of bones in a human spine). The length of these lumps corresponds to the size of the previous victim, but the &quot;spine&quot; is seriously deformed. When the mattress is cut open, there is no sign of what is causing the lumps.</p>
<p>After the primary researcher is injured in a containment breach (of another SCP), testing is paused for several weeks. During this time, one researcher complains to maintenance about bumps in the hallway outside of SCPs room. The following day, this researcher is found deceased, with their spine ripped away, lying on an old couch in their office. Apparently, SCP-XXXX is a creature that moved from the mattress to the couch through the floor when ignored.</p>
<p>When it was discovered that the SCP could move, researchers investigated locations near the mattress for potential causes of the anomaly. They discovered that an elderly man with lordosis (swayback) passed away near the murdered child. He was known to say he'd sell his soul to have a young person's spine again. Relationship not yet established</p>

