<p>Place holder, will finish this review at the ER&#8230;</p>
<hr />
<p>The agony that sent me to the hospital was so severe that I was able to get nothing done while I was there, but now I am at home again, with a mild analgesic to numb the area in question so let me try once more.</p>
<hr />
<p>Initial Impressions: And this is why this green-lighting process is stupid and counter-productive: this is already ready to be written up as an article and were it within my power you would have your first Green-Light.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: This concept is unique and AFAIK, we have nothing like it: I find it solid and compelling it grabs you and doesn't let-go.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: This story is original and informative, I would like to see where it goes. Of especially great merit is that the primary researcher looses lock and this is when things go wrong.</p>
<p>Hook: Crossed out containment procedures is a nice touch, but might be slightly over-used: I advise caution.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: The personal connection might be extraneous, but it was interesting to read.</p>
<p>In Summary: This should already have been green-lighted; I find it baffling that it's not.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Let me re-iterate: I am half-mad with pain as I write this; you should not take this as gospel.</p>

