<p>So, although I recognize that you’ve put a lot of effort and energy into this concept&#8230; it feels like a well laid out “murder monster”</p>
<p>In terms of adding narrative, consider the following questions and in answering them, edit your original idea to reflect:</p>
<ul>
<li>what is the overall arc of this story? Merely the discovery of the monster, or is there more to it?</li>
<li>Often times a shallow seeming horror story can be a vehicle for discussion of larger thematic elements&#8230; what do you want your story to communicate to the reader? What’s the take away?</li>
<li>Consider adding some depth to this creature&#8230; why does it do this?</li>
<li>From who’s perspective is the story going to be? And why should the reader care? (How will you engage the reader to be invested in these events?)</li>
</ul>

